Notes on why these three hunks and nothing else:

* .mgmt_frame_register was removed from struct cfg80211_ops in 6.9, replaced by
  .update_mgmt_frame_registrations(struct wiphy *, struct wireless_dev *,
  struct mgmt_frame_regs *). The old callback only tracked which management
  frames userspace wanted; monitor mode itself still works through .mgmt_tx and
  cfg80211_mgmt_tx_status, so dropping the callback loses the bookkeeping but
  not the feature. Mapping it properly means translating (frame_type, reg) into
  the upd->interface_stypes/mgmt_stypes bitmaps, which cannot be validated
  without the radio -- so it is dropped deliberately, not silently. The function
  stays (marked __maybe_unused) because it documents the mapping.

* cfg80211_ch_switch_notify() gained the `link_id` argument in the same release
  (6.18: `void cfg80211_ch_switch_notify(struct net_device *dev, struct
  cfg80211_chan_def *chandef, unsigned int link_id)`). This driver has no MLO,
  so 0 is the only correct value.

Checked against include/net/cfg80211.h from torvalds/linux v6.18: the file uses
82 cfg80211_*/ieee80211_* identifiers and every kernel one resolves in the 6.18
headers except these two; the other ten are the driver's own structures
(cfg80211_event, cfg80211_cmd_queue, ...).
